==Latin==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|la|uacuus}} {{qualifier|most Latin texts use the same character for 'u' and 'v'}}

===Etymology===
From {{suffix|la|vacō|uus|t1=I am empty, void|t2=adjective-forming suffix}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|vacuus|eccl=yes}}

===Adjective===
{{la-adj-1&2|vacuus|vacua|vacuum}}

# {{l|en|empty}}, {{l|en|vacant}}, {{l|en|unoccupied}}
#: ''Fēmina dīxit pōculum '''vacuum''' esse.''
#:: The woman said that the cup was '''empty'''.
#* {{Q|la|Jerome|Vulgate|Genesis|1|2|quote=terra autem erat inanis et '''vacua''' et tenebrae super faciem abyssi et spiritus Dei ferebatur super aquas|trans=And the earth was void and '''empty''', and darkness was upon the face of the deep; and the spirit of God moved over the waters.}}
# {{l|en|devoid}} or {{l|en|free}} of, {{l|en|without}}
# {{lb|la|of time}} {{l|en|free}}, unoccupied

